Origin: the 2026-08-23 supab5 A/B. Every row failed with "GPU llama-server
failed for Qwen3.5-9B-MTP" while the loaded, serving model was Qwen3.8-27B
(the harness keeps repo_substr at its frozen 9B pin by design; model_path
from CARNOT_ARC_GGUF_PATH wins at load). The label pointed the investigation
at model resolution; the true cause — an external SIGTERM from
ExperimentTemplate.kill_gpu_zombies(), see REQ-INFRA-079, fixed in the
sibling change — sat unread in the server stderr tail.

- _effective_model_label(): model_path basename first, repo_substr fallback;
  same rule liveness_witness() already uses for generator_model_declared.
- Both "GPU llama-server failed" sites use it; message prefix unchanged.
- _server_death_signature(): reads the launched server's stderr tail and
  names the external-termination signature ("cleaning up before exit" /
  "Received second interrupt"); _note_server_failure appends it, so the row
  note carries the smoking gun. Never raises; absent/unreadable log -> no hint.
- Rejected alternative: changing the harness's frozen repo_substr pin. That
  pin is deliberate (recorded-history meaning); only the LABEL was wrong.

Tests: tests/python/test_arc_generator_failure_note_2026_08_23.py
(SCENARIO-ARC-WMTE-6670-1..3), each proven by deletion (label mutation RED,
hint-append mutation RED, restores byte-identical). 120 generator-surface
tests pass.

